<h2 id="embeds">External webpages and blocked content</h2>

A Webpage card can embed an external page, or a file from `/local`. The theme cannot control that page's typography, accessibility, availability, content policy or sign-in. Browsers block some pages from being embedded, and a page served over HTTP cannot be embedded in Home Assistant over HTTPS. The card's `disable_sandbox` and `allow_open_top_navigation` options make the frame less secure. Do not use them to make a frame load.

Name the provider and the purpose of the page, keep the native security settings, and offer an ordinary link when embedding is blocked or unsuitable. Say that opening the page leaves Home Assistant. Do not describe it as a local setting.

Keep tokens, passwords and household identifiers out of example URLs. Do not load a sensitive external feed automatically on a shared display. A blank frame is a loading or failure problem. It does not show that the household has no data. The example below uses a fixed unavailable state and a public documentation link. It does not load a third-party frame.

